---
title: Watcher and watcher event lifecycle (implemented)
---
stateDiagram-v2
  direction LR
  state "Watcher (WatcherPhase)" as W {
    [*] --> Active : watch.create commits watcher and launches process in one write
    Active --> Settled : tick settle_observed records the outcome and one event
    Active --> Stopping : watch.cancel with stopProcess and a live run
    Active --> Cancelled : watch.cancel without stopProcess, or owner session ended or project archived
    Stopping --> Settled : the stop is observed and the outcome is recorded
    Settled --> [*]
    Cancelled --> [*]
  }
  state "Event (WatchEventState)" as E {
    [*] --> Pending : recorded with the watcher state change
    Pending --> Delivered : deliver_pending appends a host notice to the session and marks it in one write
    Delivered --> Acknowledged : end_turn of the carrying turn with completed true
    Delivered --> Delivered : the carrying turn ends otherwise, so the next turn carries it again
    Acknowledged --> [*]
  }
  note right of W
    Open means Active or Stopping.
    Outcome kinds: Succeeded, Failed, Cancelled, TimedOut, Interrupted, Lost, Uncertain.
    A Timer settles at due_at_ms. A Probe waits with doubling backoff up to 8 intervals.
    A polling watcher settles TimedOut at its maximum lifetime.
    close_at_shutdown ends a stopped process watcher as Interrupted.
  end note
  note right of E
    Events wait, undelivered, while the owner root is paused or held.
    Events of an ended session are never delivered.
    The backup check delivers a missed Pending event under its own event ID
    and records WatcherBackupCatch.
  end note
